According to a new report from Intel Market Research, the global Paper for Publishing market was valued at USD 65,749 million in 2025 and is projected to reach USD 74,836 million by 2034, exhibiting a robust CAGR of 1.4% during the forecast period (2025–2034). This growth is propelled by steady advertising spend, persistent demand from education sectors, and a pronounced shift toward environmentally certified paper grades.
What is Paper for Publishing?
Paper for Publishing refers to specialized grades designed for books, magazines, newspapers and other printed media. Frequently it incorporates clay‑coated layers-using kaolin or calcium carbonate-to improve surface smoothness, brightness and ink holdout, thereby delivering high‑resolution image reproduction, accurate colour fidelity and enhanced readability for mass‑printing applications.
